[2018-11-08T09:55:54Z | ravitejaveeragandam | comment]
Hi,

I taken the latest software and started working. Observed a strange behavior.

I will explain my scenario first
On power on i use to send 9 packets of data, each size of 14 bytes. And my program waits for response for the 9 packets what i sent. Once it get response it will send next packets.

With earlier software version 1.2.8, i am able to receive the response message and send the data(10th packet) one or two times and gets hang in "DoTimeouts".

But with software version 1.2.10, i am able to receive correct response for one of the 9 packets which i am sending and able to place next one packet data in IOT buffer to transfer. But from IOT i am unable to send the data to Server(not able to receive in TWIN device explorer). And also i confirmed that "SendConfirmationCallback" is not getting called.

Is there anything extra care i need to take in new software? I have doubt like did connection gets closed once after first transaction? Because every time i restart i am able to send the data.. Once after first transaction i am not able send data.

Note: Using function "IoTHubClient_LL_GetSendStatus" i got the status as "IOTHUB_CLIENT_SEND_STATUS_BUSY". 

Control is not coming out of  below loop
do
          {
            IoTHubClient_LL_DoWork(IOTHubClientHandle);
            ThreadAPI_Sleep(10);

            IoTHubClient_LL_GetSendStatus(IOTHubClientHandle , &iothub_send_status);

          } while (iothub_send_status == IOTHUB_CLIENT_SEND_STATUS_BUSY);

