[2019-01-23T17:36:29Z | jebrando | comment]
@AndWass This line of code is the concerning line:
```C
prov_dev_set_symmetric_key_info("", "");
```

It looks like the symm key is getting overwritten by blank quotes.  This would make sense in that AMQP and MQTT are different and timing would be different.  Take out that blank line and it should work.

[2019-01-23T18:47:58Z | AndWass | comment]
@jebrando So basicly it is impossible to query the DPS for multiple devices using multiple symmetric keys without running into race conditions? Because that is what I need to be able to do

[2019-01-23T19:45:54Z | AndWass | comment]
@jebrando On further code review; wouldn't a call to `Prov_Device_Create` call `Prov_Device_LL_Create` which calls `hsm_client_set_symm_key_info` on line 297 in `prov_auth_client.c`. Arguments to this function will call `prov_dev_get_symm_registration_name` and `prov_dev_get_symmetric_key` and make deep copies of the resulting keys. Since `prov_dev_set_symmetric_key_info("", "");` is called after `Prov_Device_Create` shouldn't deep copies of the keys provided in the first call to `prov_dev_set_symmetric_key_info` (with actual keys) be used and thus the explanation not sufficient?

Please correct me if this analysis is incorrect though.

I will try it tomorrow without that call to empty the keys though just to be sure.

