-A PREROUTING -i eth0 -p tcp -m tcp --dport 4050 -j DNAT --to-destination 172.16.0.5:3040;
is correct. You have specified the internal port to be 3040. This is the port at the destination host 172.16.0.5. This is a port on the host inside the firewall you are trying to reach from outside. On the other hand, the --dport parameter is a port on a gateway that you specify when you are trying to reach the 172.16.0.5:3040.

